          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A set of numbers is a ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "geometric progression",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " if the ratio between successive terms is constant. For example, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\{2,6,18\\}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is a geometric progression with common ratio 3.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-q14-given",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The polynomial equation ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x^3-7x^2+14x-8=0",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " has its roots in geometric progression.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let the roots be $\\dfrac{\\alpha}{r}$, $\\alpha$ and $\\alpha r$, where $r$ is the common ratio.\nUse product of roots to find a root.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=2$.",
          "worked": "Using the product of roots:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\alpha}{r}\\times\\alpha\\times\\alpha r&=8\\\\\\alpha^3&=8\\\\\\alpha&=2\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Therefore, completely factorise $x^3-7x^2+14x-8=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-2)(x-4)(x-1)=0$.",
          "worked": "Since 2 is a root, $x-2$ is a linear factor. Long division gives\n$$\\begin{array}{r|rrrr} &x^2-5x+4&&&\\\\x-2&x^3&-7x^2&+14x&-8\\\\ &x^3&-2x^2&&\\\\\\hline &&-5x^2&+14x&\\\\ &&-5x^2&+10x&\\\\\\hline &&&4x&-8\\\\ &&&4x&-8\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^3-7x^2+14x-8&=(x-2)(x^2-5x+4)\\\\&=(x-2)(x-4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}$$\nHence the equation is $(x-2)(x-4)(x-1)=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Therefore, find the roots of $x^3-7x^2+14x-8=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,2,4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-4)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=2,\\ 4,\\ 1\\end{aligned}$$\nThe roots are $1,2,4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      }
    ]
  },
